From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:32:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Speech::setParams: refuse speeds that give no or too long
 frames

A speed of 0 or below gave klatt frames of no or a negative number of samples, so SpeechInstance asked new[] for a negative size or played nothing; a speed past the int range of 11025 * speed did the same. Speeds now give frames of 1 to 11025 samples (up to 1000 ms); others return INVALID_PARAMETER and change nothing.
---
 src/audiosource/speech/soloud_speech.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/speech/soloud_speech.cpp b/src/audiosource/speech/soloud_speech.cpp
index 6affec7..51cfb81 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/speech/soloud_speech.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/speech/soloud_speech.cpp
@@ -106,6 +106,10 @@ namespace SoLoud
 
 	result Speech::setParams(unsigned int aBaseFrequency, float aBaseSpeed, float aBaseDeclination, int aBaseWaveform)
 	{
+		// klatt renders frames of (int)(11025 * speed) / 1000 samples: take
+		// the speeds that give 1 to 11025 (up to 1000 ms).
+		if (!(aBaseSpeed > 0.0f && aBaseSpeed <= 1000.0f) || (int)(11025 * aBaseSpeed) / 1000 < 1)
+			return INVALID_PARAMETER;
 		mBaseFrequency = aBaseFrequency;
 		mBaseSpeed = aBaseSpeed;
 		mBaseDeclination = aBaseDeclination;
